.TH CLOCK 1 "2026-06-13" "clock" "Terminal Clock"
.SH NAME
clock \- terminal dashboard: clock and machine monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clock
[\fB--help\fR] [\fB--once\fR] [\fB--all\fR] [\fB--gpu\fR] [\fB--fan\fR] [\fB--sunday-start\fR] [\fB--widgets\fR \fIlist\fR] [\fB--ip-refresh\fR [\fIn\fR]] [\fB--weather-refresh\fR [\fIn\fR]] [\fBauto\fR|\fBtext\fR|\fBascii\fR|\fBsixel\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clock
displays a real-time dashboard: a large digital clock centered on the
terminal and a right-side information bar showing system metrics.
.B clock
gathers all data from /proc, /sys, and netlink (rtnetlink + nl80211) without invoking external binaries.
Public IPv4/IPv6 addresses are fetched periodically from api.ipify.org
over HTTP. Weather data is fetched from wttr.in over HTTP.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B auto
Auto-detect the best display mode (default). If stdout is a terminal
with sixel support, sixel mode is used. If stdout is a terminal without
sixel, ascii mode is used. Otherwise, text mode is used.
.TP
.B text
Plain text output, one metric per line. Suitable for piping to files or
other programs.
.TP
.B ascii
Large digital clock using Unicode block characters plus a right-side
info bar with Unicode icons for wireless, weather, battery, etc.
.TP
.B sixel
Sixel graphics clock digits (bitmapped from dot-matrix patterns) with
regular terminal text info bar. No sixel icons.
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Print usage summary to stdout and exit 0.
.TP
.B \-\-once, \-o
Print output once and exit. No 1-second loop.
.TP
.B \-\-all, \-a
Enable \fB--gpu\fR and \fB--fan\fR together. Only effective when
\fB--widgets\fR is not given.
.TP
.B \-\-gpu, \-g
Enable GPU monitoring: usage, core/memory clock, memory usage,
temperature, fan. Only effective when \fB--widgets\fR is not given.
.TP
.B \-\-fan, \-f
Enable motherboard fan speeds and motherboard temperatures (merged,
no separate --temp flag). Only effective when \fB--widgets\fR is not
given.
.TP
.B \-\-sunday\-start, \-S
Calendar week starts on Sunday instead of Monday.
.TP
.B \-\-widgets \fIlist\fR, \-w
Comma-separated list of widget names controlling sidebar content and
order. Overrides \fB--gpu\fR, \fB--fan\fR, and \fB--all\fR. Empty
string disables sidebar entirely (full-screen clock). Valid widget
names: DATE, CPU, GPU, MEM, FAN, BAT, UP, STO, NET, WEATHER, CAL.
.TP
.B \-\-ip\-refresh [\fIn\fR], \-I
Set public IP refresh interval in seconds. Default: 86400 (24 hours).
If no argument is given, the default interval is used.
.TP
.B \-\-weather\-refresh [\fIn\fR], \-W
Set weather refresh interval in seconds. Default: 1800 (30 minutes).
If no argument is given, the default interval is used.
.SH WIDGETS
The sidebar is built from named widget sections. The default order
(when \fB--widgets\fR is not given) is:
.PP
DATE, CPU, GPU, MEM, FAN, BAT, UP, STO, NET, WEATHER, CAL
.PP
With \fB--widgets\fR, only the listed widgets appear, in the given
order. Data sources are only read for active widgets (lazy reads).
.SH DISPLAY SECTIONS
Clock (center-left or full-width when sidebar is empty), date,
CPU usage/load/freq/governor/temperature, GPU stats, memory usage,
motherboard fans and temperatures, battery state and icon, uptime,
storage throughput and per-mount usage, network throughput per
interface and wireless signal and IP addresses, weather icon and
temperature, and month calendar.
.SH FILES
.I /proc/stat
.I /proc/meminfo
.I sysinfo()
.I /proc/self/mountinfo
.I /sys/block/*/stat
.I /sys/fs/cgroup/memory.current
.I /sys/fs/cgroup/memory.max
.I /sys/class/power_supply/BAT*/type
.I /sys/class/power_supply/BAT*/capacity
.I /sys/class/power_supply/BAT*/status
.I /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu*/cpufreq/
.I /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cpufreq/scaling_governor
.I /sys/devices/platform/coretemp.0/hwmon/hwmon*/temp1_input
.I /sys/bus/pci/drivers/k10temp/*/hwmon/hwmon*/temp1_input
.I /sys/class/drm/card[0-9]/device/
.I /sys/class/hwmon/hwmon*/
.I (rtnetlink) routes, addresses/link dumps
.I (rtnetlink) address/link event monitor (NETLINK_ROUTE, multicast)
.I (nl80211) wireless signal and SSID (NETLINK_GENERIC)
.I (SIOCETHTOOL) ETHTOOL_GLINKSETTINGS for wired link speed
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success. An unrecognized argument prints an error message to stderr
and exits with code 1.
